# Command: AI (Set frame(s))
# Radio: Kenwood TS-590S / TS-590SG
# Title (cover, verbatim): "TS-590S TS-590SG / PC CONTROL COMMAND / Reference Guide"
# Printed revision: NONE printed; cover carries "JVCKENWOOD Corporation" and
#   "January/30/2019".
# Source page: printed folio "- 3 -"  ==  PDF page 4 of 35
# Charts used: the Set chart of the AI block (Read and Answer charts recorded below
#   for completeness of the position map)
# Derivation date: 05/09/2026
# NO code, no generator, no other file and no other document was consulted.
#
# COUNTED FRAME LENGTHS (two independent counts of the printed numbered ruler):
#   AI Set    = 4 positions
#   AI Read   = 3 positions
#   AI Answer = 4 positions
#
# CHARTS, position by position:
#   Set:     1 A  2 I  3 P1  4 ;      (5..10 empty)
#   Read:    1 A  2 I  3 ;            (4..10 empty)
#   Answer:  1 A  2 I  3 P1  4 ;      (5..10 empty)
#
# Field map (Set):
#   pos 1-2  "AI"
#   pos 3    P1  (one character)
#   pos 4    ";"
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LEGEND, VERBATIM (the complete right-hand column; block description reads
# "Sets and reads the Auto Information (AI) function ON/ OFF."):
#
#   [TS-590S / TS-590SG common]
#   Parameters:
#   P1
#     0:  AI OFF
#     2:  AI ON (without backup)
#     4:  AI ON (with backup)
#
#   * When AI is ON, the respective response command is output
#     when the parameter is changed by the command with the
#     response command.
#   * When AI is ON by setting P1 parameter to 2 and the power is
#     turned to OFF, AI is also turned to OFF.
#   * P1 parameter 4 (with backup) is supported from the firmware
#     version 2.00 in TS-590S
#
#   (Transcribed exactly as printed.  Only 0, 2 and 4 are printed; 1 and 3 are not
#    listed at all.  See FINDING F9 - not resolved here.)
#
# POSITIONS THE CHART PRINTS AS FIXED / "Always": NONE in the AI block.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BYTES WHOSE VALUE THE MANUAL DOES NOT DETERMINE  -> INHERITED-ASSUMED
#   NONE.  Every byte of every vector below is determined by the printed chart and
#   the printed legend.
#
# Hardware status: UNVERIFIED for every vector in this file.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VECTORS  (name <TAB> frame bytes verbatim)
#
ai590_set_off	AI0;
ai590_set_on_without_backup	AI2;
ai590_set_on_with_backup	AI4;
ai590_read	AI;
ai590_answer_off	AI0;
ai590_answer_on_without_backup	AI2;
ai590_answer_on_with_backup	AI4;
